WLIB.add('stage', [
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'My grandfather fixed watches. He told me every watch keeps its own time and the job is to talk it round, not force it. I tried that with him at the end. He kept his own time to the last minute.'],
  ['*', '*', 'mono', 1, 'I have worked so hard to get here. Nobody believed in me. But now I will show them all.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I bought a plant to prove I could keep something alive. The plant is thriving. It is thriving out of spite. It looks at me every morning like it has been told something about me.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You keep saying "we" as if I was in the room when it was decided. I was in the car park. I could see the window. I watched all of you nod.'],
  ['Thriller', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I know what was in the envelope. I know because I put it there. What I do not know is who took it out, and why they put it back.'],
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'Everything I loved has been taken from me. I have nothing left. What is the point of going on?'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 3, 'I have been on hold for two hours. The music is very good. I have started to have feelings about the music. If somebody answers now, I will be devastated.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I still set the table for two. I know. I know. But the drawer has two of everything, and it seems rude to the forks.'],
  ['Crime', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You want a confession. Fine. I confess I liked him. I confess I lent him the car. I confess I knew where he was going and I filled the tank anyway.'],
  ['Romance', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I think I am falling in love with you. I have never felt this way about anyone before.'],
  ['Period', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I was in service in this house for thirty years. I know which stair creaks and which drawer sticks and which of the portraits was painted over a different face. The family know none of it. It was never theirs to know.'],
  ['War', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'They gave us a pamphlet about what to do if the worst happened. Step one was keep calm. Step two was a blank line, for you to write your own. Most of us wrote our mothers\' names.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I always wanted to be the sort of person who has a signature dish. I have a signature sandwich. It is cheese and it is fine. People ask for it. I think they are being kind.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'You lied to me. You have been lying to me this whole time. How could you do this to me?'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'On the station, they ration showers, so I keep a list of the people I have shared a shower slot with. Two hundred and six names. I have only ever spoken to four. I know all of them by how long they leave the water running.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'My mother has started texting in full sentences with full stops. Every message is like being sent to the headmaster. "I hope you are well." Full stop. I have never been less well.'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I learned to drive at night so nobody would see me get it wrong. I still drive best at night. In the daytime there are too many people watching, even if they are not.'],
  ['Horror', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'It started with the doors. I would close them at night and in the morning they would be open, just a hand\'s width. Not wide. Just enough to see through.'],
  ['Western', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'My father said a man is known by the fences he mends. He died with half the north fence still down. I have mended it twice since. I keep leaving one post loose, so he will not be finished.'],
  ['*', '*', 'mono', 1, 'Life is short. You have to grab every chance you get. That is what I have learned.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I keep my school reports in a shoebox. "Could try harder," every single year. I am fifty-one. I have tried harder. I would like somebody to write that down.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 3, 'I was not always a {JOB}. I was going to be an astronaut. Then I was going to be a pilot. Then I was going to work at the airport. Then I flew once, on holiday, and was sick, and here we are.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'You call it a curse. I call it the only promise anyone ever kept to me. They said I would never sleep, and I have not. Not for {YEARS}.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'Sit down. No, the other chair. That one is for people I like.'],
  ['Musical', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I have always loved to sing. Singing makes me feel free. One day I will sing on a big stage.'],
  ['Romance', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'You used to leave the radio on when you went out, so the cat would not be lonely. You have been gone a year. I have not turned it off once. The cat has heard every news bulletin there is.'],
  ['Thriller', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'The thing about a small town is that everyone knows your car. So I took the bus. Nobody in this town has ever looked at the bus.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I got your postcard. It said "Wish you were here." I would like to know where you were, exactly, so I can work out whether you meant it.'],
  ['Crime', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'I did it. I killed him. And I would do it again.'],
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'There is a particular silence a house has after an argument. Not the absence of noise. The presence of everything nobody said. I grew up in that silence. I could draw you a map of it.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I went to a wedding where they released doves. One of the doves did not want to be released. It sat on the cake. It looked me dead in the eye. I have never related to anything more.'],
  ['War', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'When I came home, my mother had kept my room exactly as it was. Same sheets, same books, same boy in the photographs. I slept on the floor. The bed belonged to him.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'My grandmother told me never to trust a person who does not like soup. It is the only advice she gave me. I have never once known what to do with it. I have also never been wrong.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'They told us the colony would be self-sufficient within five years. That was nineteen years ago. We have stopped counting the years. We count the tins.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'I am sick of everyone telling me what to do. This is my life and I will make my own choices.'],
  ['Superhero', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'You think the hard part is the burning buildings. The hard part is Tuesday. Nothing is on fire and I still have to choose what to have for lunch, like everyone else, and I am no good at it.'],
  ['Period', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I have read the will. I read it before he died, while he was at church. I put it back in the drawer the right way up. He never knew. I would like you to remember that, before you call me a thief.'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'When the phone rings at night now, I do not get up. I let it ring. Whatever it is, it has already happened, and I want five more minutes of not knowing.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 1, 'Why does this always happen to me? I am the unluckiest person in the world!'],
  ['Romance', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I said yes because you asked in front of everyone. I want you to know that. I want you to know there was a second where I nearly said "Can we talk about this later" in front of your entire family.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'Dad taught me to whistle with two fingers. I never got it. When he was in the hospital I practised in the car park for a week so I could do it for him. The first time it worked, I was alone, and I just stood there with my fingers in my mouth, crying.'],
  ['Horror', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'Mother always said to count the stairs going up, and count them going down, and if the numbers ever disagreed, to stay exactly where I was. I am on the landing. I have been on the landing since Tuesday.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'I know what you did. Don\'t try to deny it. I know everything.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'Everyone wants to be the chosen one until they find out what the chosen one is chosen for. Mostly paperwork. Prophecies come with an astonishing amount of paperwork.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I have a theory that everyone has exactly one perfect parking space in their lifetime. I used mine at nineteen, outside a shop I did not need, on a day when I had nowhere to be.'],
  ['Crime', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I was a good thief. I want that on record. I never took anything anybody would miss on a Sunday. Silver from the back of the drawer. The watch nobody wound. I stole the things people had already stopped loving.'],
  ['Drama', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'Starting today, everything is going to be different. I am going to change my life.'],
  ['Thriller', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I do not hate you. Hate is expensive and I am a careful person. I have simply put you in a column, and I review the column once a year.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I have kept every birthday card you sent. You always wrote the same thing. "Have a good one." Twenty-two cards. I read them all last night and realised you meant it every time.'],
  ['Western', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'You ride in on a borrowed horse with a borrowed name and you want to borrow my daughter as well. I lend nothing on a Sunday, stranger. Come back on Monday and we will see if you are still here.'],
  ['Martial arts', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'My teacher said the hardest technique is the one you never use. I did not understand. I thought he meant a secret move. He meant the one where you walk away.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 2, 'I joined a book club to meet people. It is just me and two men who have both read a different book. Every week. They seem very happy. I have read four books I do not care about.'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'Nobody cares about me. Nobody ever has. I am completely alone.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'The ship\'s computer and I have been alone together for three years. It knows every joke I have ever told. Last week, for the first time, it laughed at one before I finished. I have not felt that lonely in years.'],
  ['Period', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'I was taught to curtsey before I was taught to read. I can do it in any shoes, on any floor, holding a tray. My mistress says I am the most graceful girl in the house. Nobody has ever asked what I would do with my legs if I did not have to bend them.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I am going to say this once, and then I am going to make tea, and you are going to drink it, and we are never going to talk about it again.'],
  ['Romance', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I am going to tell you something and you are not allowed to laugh. I practised asking you out on the cat. The cat said yes. The cat was very enthusiastic. You have a lot to live up to.'],
  ['War', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'War is terrible. I have seen things no one should ever have to see.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I think adulthood is just discovering, one at a time, that all the grown-ups in your life were guessing. My father, guessing. The doctor, guessing. I am guessing right now. Look at me. I have no idea.'],
  ['Horror', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'Do not look at the window. I mean it. Look at me. Keep looking at me and tell me something about your day.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I am not good at anything. I tried cooking, singing and dancing and I was terrible at all of them!'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I was the last one in the family to learn the truth. They told the dog before they told me. I know because the dog looked at me differently all that week.'],
  ['Crime', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I am not going to run. I want you to know that. I am going to finish this coffee, I am going to wash the cup, and then I am going to walk out of that door at a perfectly ordinary speed, and you are going to let me.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'I was a dragon, once. Not in the way you mean. I was the thing they told children about to make them come home before dark. Now I am the reason they come home. I cannot tell you which is the worse job.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I have done the maths. I have done it three times, on three different calculators. It comes out the same. One of us is not going to be here next year.'],
  ['Musical', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'Every song I know, I learned from somebody who is gone now. My mother\'s hymns. My uncle\'s drinking songs. I am a sort of attic. Nobody visits but everything is still in here.'],
  ['Superhero', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I have special powers now. I must use them to help the people of {CITY}.'],
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I used to think forgiving someone would feel like putting something down. It does not. It feels like carrying it differently. Same weight, other arm.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 2, 'I have entered a competition to name the new {CITY} ferry. My suggestion was "Unsinkable". The council have written back. They said that was asking for it.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 1, 'I wish I had told you how much you meant to me before it was too late.'],
  ['Thriller', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'The trouble with a perfect alibi is that you have to remember it perfectly. I have been remembering mine for {YEARS}. I could tell it to you in my sleep. I have, in fact. That is how she found out.'],
  ['Romance', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'You asked me once what I would save in a fire. I said the photographs. That was a lie. I would have saved the chair you always sat in, because the photographs are of you and the chair still has you in it.'],
  ['Period', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'My mother arranged three suitors for me this season. One talks only of horses, one only of money, one only of his mother. I have asked if I might marry the horse.'],
  ['War', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'Everyone wants to know what it was like. I tell them it was cold. They are disappointed. It was cold. Nobody will believe how much of it was just being cold.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'This is the most important decision of my life. I have to get it right.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I talk to my car. Everybody talks to their car. But I listen, as well. That is the bit people find worrying.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You keep asking if I am the original. I do not know how to answer that. I remember being born. I remember the factory. Both memories are equally vivid and only one of them comes with a serial number.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I have been to so many leaving parties at work that I have started to feel I should leave, just to be fair to the cake.'],
  ['Horror', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'Something is in this house with us. I can feel it. We have to get out now.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'There is a bench in {CITY} with my brother\'s name on it. People sit on it to eat their lunch. They have no idea. I like that. He would have hated a memorial anyone actually looked at.'],
  ['Western', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I have buried eleven men on this hill. I say the same words over each one. I have never once believed them. Out here, the words are not for God. They are for the horse, so he knows we are done and can walk home.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I am not frightened of you. I am frightened of the version of me that will be standing here in ten minutes if you keep talking.'],
  ['Crime', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I am the best detective in the city. No case is too hard for me.'],
  ['Martial arts', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'Ten thousand times I have done this move. Ten thousand times in an empty room. Today there is someone in the room. Let us see if the move noticed.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 3, 'I am going to say the most frightening sentence a man can hear. Ready? "Before you go, I have one small question about the spreadsheet."'],
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I know exactly how long it takes to drive from here to the hospital. Eleven minutes, if the lights are with you. I have driven it so many times I could do it with my eyes shut. Some nights I nearly have.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I may be small, but I have a big heart. I will save the kingdom, I promise!'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'The day my mother forgot my name, she still knew I took two sugars. I have decided that is the more important fact. I have decided a lot of things like that recently.'],
  ['Romance', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'Do not say it. Whatever it is. If you say it, I will have to answer, and I have been practising the wrong answer for weeks.'],
  ['Period', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'I have been wronged by this family. They will pay for what they have done to me.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'People say I am competitive. I am not competitive. I simply have never lost, and I would like it to stay that way, at board games, with my nephew, who is six.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I was born on the ship. I have never seen weather. When the old ones talk about rain, I imagine it as something like applause.'],
  ['Thriller', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I have a rule. I never ask a question I do not already know the answer to. So I am not going to ask where you were last night. I am going to ask whether the hotel did a nice breakfast.'],
  ['Drama', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I finally did it! I passed my exam! All my hard work has paid off!'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I sleep with the light on. I am forty-four. I do not want to talk about why. I want you to leave it on when you go.'],
  ['War', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'Corporal Ellis carried a harmonica the whole way across that country. Never played it. Said he was saving it for the day it was over. It is in my drawer now. I have never played it either. It does not seem over.'],
  ['Horror', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I am not saying the house is haunted. I am saying that every morning there is one more slipper by the bed than there are feet in this family, and I have stopped counting the feet.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 2, 'I was voted Most Likely To Succeed at school. I would like to find the people who voted and ask them what, specifically, they had in mind.'],
  ['Crime', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I identified him by his shoes. They asked me to look at his face but I could not, so I looked at his feet. He never could tie a double knot. He was still wearing the single bow I tied for him that morning.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I love my friends so much. They are always there for me no matter what.'],
  ['Musical', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I can sing every part of every song in this town. The baritone, the soprano, the bit the drummer shouts. Ask me to sing my own part and I have no idea which one it is.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I can tell when you are about to lie. You put your keys down. Every time. You put your keys on the table and then you say something kind. Put them in your pocket. Go on. Now try.'],
  ['Superhero', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I saved {CITY} four times last year. Nobody knows my name. The one time I did not save it, I am on every front page.'],
  ['Romance', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I have loved you since the day you returned my library book. Not since you returned it. Since you told me it was overdue. You were very stern about it. I had never been told off so beautifully.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'I will not let you destroy everything I have worked for.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'My father\'s idea of a heart-to-heart is to hand me a screwdriver and stand next to me while we both look at a shelf.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I kept your voicemail. Twenty-three seconds. You are ringing to ask if I want anything from the shop. I have listened to it so many times I have started to answer. Yes. Bread. Come home.'],
]);
WLIB.add('stage', [
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'I have made so many mistakes in my life. I wish I could take them all back.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 3, 'I am the only person in my family who can work the television. This is not a skill. This is a sentence. I will be called to that remote control on Christmas Day until I die.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'The first thing I ever bought with my own money was a blue umbrella. I lost it on a bus that same afternoon. I have been looking for it on every bus since, which is a stupid way to live and also, I think, the only way I know.'],
  ['Thriller', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'Someone is following me. I know it. I can feel them watching me everywhere I go.'],
  ['Period', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I learned to write so I could read the letters he sent from the front. By the time I could read them, he had stopped sending them. I read the old ones now. My handwriting is better than his ever was.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'They let us keep one object from Earth. I brought a stone from my mother\'s garden. It is the only stone on this planet that has ever been rained on. I hold it during the dust storms.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I am not asking you to choose. I am telling you that you already have, last March, in the car, when you put your hand on the gear stick instead of on mine.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I have a drawer for things that might be useful one day. Elastic bands, a single key, the instructions for a toaster I no longer own. My whole personality is in that drawer.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I cannot believe I am stuck here with you! This is the worst day ever!'],
  ['Romance', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'We met at a funeral. Not the best start, I know. But you handed me a tissue before I knew I needed one, and I have been waiting ever since for you to do something that ordinary again.'],
  ['Horror', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'When I was a child, I had an imaginary friend. He was very polite. He always waited at the end of the bed until I said he could come in. I am thirty-eight now. Last night, for the first time in years, I heard him knock.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I am going to lose this argument. I can feel it. So I would like to make one small point first, while I still have the floor: you have my coat on.'],
  ['War', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 1, 'I joined the army to make my father proud. Now I just want to go home.'],
  ['Crime', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'The money is not in the house. Do not bother. I know you will search it anyway. Start with the kitchen. Put the plates back where you find them, at least.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'Mum kept a jar of buttons. Every button from every coat any of us ever grew out of. When she died we tipped it out on the table and spent all night saying whose was whose. We were wrong about half of them. It did not matter.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I know the old spell. Of course I know it. I am the one who wrote it down. What I never told anyone is that the last line is a guess.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 2, 'I have been asked to give a speech at my own retirement do. I have been writing it for a year. It is now ninety minutes long. I have decided to stay on, so that I have time to finish it.'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'I have a secret that I have never told anyone. If people knew, they would hate me.'],
  ['Western', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I have ridden this route for twenty years. The horse knows it better than I do. Some days I think I am the one being taken for a ride, and he is too polite to mention it.'],
  ['Musical', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'Everyone in this company knows I can hit the high note. Nobody knows that every night, half a bar before it, I decide all over again whether to try.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I am a robot, but I want to learn what it means to be human.'],
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I was nine when I worked out that the shouting stopped if I was ill. So I was ill a lot. I am very good at being ill now. I am a professional. I could teach you.'],
  ['Romance', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You have been very honest with me tonight. You have said a lot of true things. I notice that none of them were about the thing you came here to say.'],
  ['Superhero', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'People ask what my power is. I can stop time for nine seconds. Nine. Everybody wants to know what I do with them. I mostly just look at my daughter.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I come from a long line of people who say "We should do this more often" and then never do it again. My grandparents said it at their wedding.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 1, 'Growing up is hard. Sometimes I wish I was a child again.'],
  ['Period', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I have been a governess in this house for four years. I have taught your children French, the harp, and how to tell when their father is lying. The French was the least useful.'],
  ['Crime', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I clean up after people. That is my job. Some people leave a mess in the kitchen. Some people leave one in the car park. I do not ask which kind you are.'],
  ['Martial arts', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I will train every day until I am the greatest fighter in the land.'],
  ['Drama', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'The first time I saw the sea I was twenty-six. I took my shoes off and walked in up to my knees in my good trousers. A woman on the beach shouted "It is cold in October, love." I shouted back that I had waited long enough.'],
  ['Thriller', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'Nobody looks at the man who empties the bins. I have been the man who empties the bins in that building for {YEARS}. I know the shape of every lie on every floor by what it throws away.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I have been counting your excuses. That was four. You have one more and then I am going to start counting mine.'],
  ['Horror', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'I am so scared. I do not want to die here. Please, somebody help us!'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 3, 'I have lived in this flat for eleven years and I have only just discovered that the switch by the door does something. It turns on a light in the flat upstairs. They have known for eleven years. They have been very patient.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'Dad never said goodbye on the phone. He just put it down when he was done. I used to hate that. Now I hold the phone after every call, waiting for the click, and it is never his.'],
  ['War', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'There was a farmhouse with a piano in it. The roof was gone, and the walls on one side, and somebody had played it, the night before, and left the music open on a page. We did not touch it. We walked round it like it was a man asleep.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I have been a knight for thirty years. I have slain two dragons and an extremely large goose. The goose is the one people ask about.'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I have started to rehearse your funeral. Not because I want it. Because I know I will be the one who has to do the speaking, and I want to be able to do it without looking at the paper.'],
  ['Romance', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'You are the most amazing person I have ever met. I want to spend the rest of my life with you.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'The ship has lied to me before. Small lies. The temperature. Whether it is morning. Today it told me there was no one else on board and it said it so gently that I went to check the airlocks.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I tried meditation. You sit and think about nothing. I sat and thought about how I was doing at thinking about nothing. I got a three out of ten. I was quite pleased.'],
  ['Crime', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'He taught me to pick locks on the back door of our own house. Said a person should always be able to get home. I have been in a hundred houses since. Not once did it feel like getting home.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'I have to tell you something important. Please do not be angry with me.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'My sister and I have had the same argument every Christmas for twenty years. Neither of us remembers what it was originally about. We just know our lines. It is the most reliable thing in our family.'],
  ['Period', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'The master says I am lucky to have a roof. I have counted the slates on that roof from my bed. There are four hundred and twelve, and nine are missing, and every one of the missing nine is above me.'],
  ['Musical', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'When I sing, all my problems disappear. Music is my whole life.'],
  ['Horror', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'The thing about the voice on the baby monitor is not that it is there. It is that it is singing the lullaby I made up. Nobody else knows that lullaby. I never sang it out loud. I only ever hummed it.'],
  ['Western', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You can have the land. You can have the water rights and the barn and the north field. But the creek that runs past my mother\'s grave stays where it is, and you will have to ask it yourself.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I always wanted a dog. Dad said we would get one when we had a garden. We never had a garden. I have a garden now. I have a dog. I still feel I am waiting for Dad to say yes.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 1, 'Oh no! I have made a huge mess of everything again! What am I going to do?'],
  ['Thriller', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'There is a word you use when you are frightened. You do not know you use it. I have heard it three times tonight.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'Your handwriting is on every jar in this pantry. Plum, nineteen eighty. Damson, nineteen eighty-two. I cannot eat any of it. I cannot throw any of it away. I have been buying jam from the shop and putting it on the shelf beside yours, like company.'],
  ['Superhero', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I am invisible. Do you know how many parties I have been to? None. Nobody notices if you do not turn up. It turns out I am invisible even when I am not.'],
  ['Romance', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I kept the ticket from the night we met. I keep it in my wallet behind my driving licence. Every time a policeman stops me, I wonder if he will ask about it.'],
  ['Martial arts', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'My teacher broke three of my fingers when I was twelve, to teach me how to make a fist with what was left. I am grateful to him. I want you to understand how much I hate that I am grateful.'],
  ['Drama', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'I have finally found where I belong. This place feels like home.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'Light from Earth takes four years to get here. So every night I look at a planet that does not know yet that I left. Somewhere in that light, I am still waving.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'You have asked me to be honest, so I will be. I liked you better before you were honest. You were much more interesting when I had to guess.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'My nan has taken up online shopping. Every day a parcel arrives. Yesterday it was a garden gnome dressed as a lifeguard. She does not have a garden. She says he is for the bath.'],
  ['Crime', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'This city is full of crime and corruption. Someone has to stop it.'],
  ['War', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I can strip and clean a rifle in under a minute. I can do it in the dark. What I cannot do, what they never trained us for, is pick up my daughter without checking the room first.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'The prophecy said I would save the kingdom. It did not say the kingdom would be grateful. I should have read the small print. Nobody ever reads the small print on a prophecy.'],
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'You want me to say I am sorry, and I will. I am sorry. I am sorry the way the weather is sorry. It does not change what it did to the roof.'],
  ['Horror', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I know she is not real. I know that. But she sits at the end of the table and she passes me the salt before I ask for it, and nobody living has done that for me in a long time.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'Every day is a new adventure. You never know what will happen next!'],
  ['Period', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'My husband has written a book about the history of the family. It is eight hundred pages long and he has mentioned me twice, both times in reference to a carriage.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 2, 'I won a raffle. The prize was a weekend away with the man who ran the raffle. I have been trying to give it back for six months.'],
  ['Romance', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'Every summer we said we would go to the island across the bay. Every summer something came up. I went last week, by myself. It is a lovely island. There is nothing on it at all. I sat on the beach and looked back at our window.'],
  ['Thriller', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'The government is hiding the truth. I have proof. And they will do anything to stop me.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I have been the sensible one my whole life. The one who drives. The one who keeps the receipts. Tonight I would like to be the one who forgets where we parked.'],
  ['Musical', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'I played second violin for thirty-one years. Never once the solo. And I want you to know I had it learned. Every one. In case. I have a head full of solos nobody has ever heard.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'absurd', 'mono', 2, 'I am the only translator on this station who speaks both languages. I would like to tell the delegates that both sides have been insulting each other\'s hats for an hour. I am being paid by the hour.'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I am not brave. People keep saying I am brave. Brave is when you have a choice. I just did not have anywhere else to stand.'],
  ['Western', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 1, 'This land is all I have left of my family. I will never sell it.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'Whenever someone says "no offence", I brace myself, like hearing a car alarm. Nothing good has ever followed a "no offence". Nothing kind has ever been preceded by one.'],
  ['Crime', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I have never once raised my voice to you. Have you noticed? Not once, in {YEARS}. I want you to think about what I have been using instead.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 1, 'My family means everything to me. I would do anything for them.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'They built the city on my back while I slept. I woke up to roofs and bells and children. I have been holding very still ever since. You have no idea how long a thousand years is, when you are trying not to sneeze.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'Here is the deal. You tell me the truth now, and I will believe it. You tell me later, and I will believe it, but I will never believe anything else.'],
  ['Horror', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'Do you hear it? No, stop. Listen. That is not the pipes. Pipes do not breathe in.'],
  ['Superhero', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'The villain must be stopped. I am the only one who can do it.'],
  ['War', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'My brother wrote home every week. Every letter said "The food is terrible, send cake." Mother sent a cake every week for two years. When he came back he could not stand the sight of cake. He said every one had made him homesick.'],
  ['Romance', 'tense', 'mono', 2, 'I have rehearsed this so many times I have lost the sense of the words. "I love you" now sounds like the name of a town. Let me try it. I love you. There. I think it is somewhere in the north.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 1, 'Nothing ever goes right for me. Today I lost my keys, my wallet and my dignity!'],
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I have read the doctor\'s letter forty times. There is a full stop missing in the second paragraph. That is what I have fixed on. Not the word. The full stop.'],
  ['Period', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I was the one who wound the clocks in this house. All forty of them. Every Sunday. The day they let me go, I did not wind them. They will have stopped by now, one by one, in the order I always wound them.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'We have to get off this planet before it is too late. Our lives depend on it.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I was always the friend who remembered birthdays. I have a little book. Last week I crossed out a name for the first time, and I did it in pencil, so it would not look so final.'],
  ['Crime', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I am not a criminal. I am a person who has been very unlucky in a series of rooms with expensive things in them.'],
  ['Martial arts', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'My mother wanted me to be a doctor. I became a fighter. In the end it is the same thing. People come to me hurt and leave me hurt in a different place.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'Thank you for the flowers. They are lilies. You know I hate lilies. You know because I told you, at the last funeral, when you brought lilies.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'My doctor told me to take up a hobby that relaxes me. I have taken up arguing with him. It is going very well. I have never been more relaxed.'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'I am a terrible person. I do not deserve to be happy.'],
  ['Thriller', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You checked the windows. Good. You checked the doors. Good. You did not check the guest bedroom, because you never had a guest. Neither did I. Until tonight.'],
  ['Musical', 'absurd', 'mono', 2, 'I was in the chorus of eleven shows. In every one, I died in the first act. Plague, war, a falling chandelier. My mother has seen me die eleven times. She says I am getting very good at it.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I am a very small wizard. I can make a cup of tea stay warm. That is all. You would be surprised how often it is exactly what is needed.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'He used to leave me notes on the fridge. "Gone out." "Back by six." "Milk." I have them all in a box. If you read them in order, they are the best letter anyone ever wrote me.'],
  ['Romance', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I fell in love with you because you said thank you to the bus driver. Every time. Even when the bus was late. I thought, there is a person who believes in other people. Please do not tell me now that you were just being polite.'],
  ['Horror', 'dark', 'mono', 1, 'The house is evil. It wants us to stay forever. We must get out before midnight!'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 3, 'I am a fully grown adult and I still do not know what you are supposed to do with your hands in a photograph. I have tried every option. In my wedding photos I am holding my own elbows.'],
  ['War', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'The orders came on thin paper. Very thin. You could see through it. I remember thinking a thing that thin should not be able to carry that many men.'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I keep a list of things that have made me happy this year. So far: a dog in a raincoat, a correct guess on a quiz, and the moment a lift arrived the instant I pressed the button. It is not a long list. I think it is a good list.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I miss weather. Not good weather. Any weather. I would give a year of my ration for a cold drizzly Tuesday in {CITY} and a bus that does not come.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'You never listen to me! You never have! For once, just hear what I am saying!'],
  ['Crime', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'My mother was a forger. She could do anyone\'s signature after one look. The only one she could never get right was her own. Every cheque she ever signed, she did it twice, and neither looked like her.'],
  ['Period', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'I am a lady of good breeding and I demand to be treated with respect.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I have a photograph of us on a beach. I do not remember the day at all. I am laughing in it. I have decided to believe the photograph.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 1, 'Being a parent is so hard! Nobody tells you how messy children are!'],
  ['Western', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'Every man who comes through this town thinks he is the first to want what is under it. I keep a list of their names on the back of the door. You can sign, if you like. Most of them did.'],
  ['Superhero', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'My superpower is that I always know where the remote is. I know it is not the one you wanted. The one you wanted went to my brother. He can fly. He never knows where anything is.'],
  ['Drama', 'dark', 'mono', 3, 'I have been to so many hospitals with you that I know which vending machines give change. I could write a guide. I think about writing it. I think that is how I will know it is over, when I want to.'],
  ['Romance', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 1, 'I let you go, and it was the biggest mistake of my life.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You want the sword? Take it. But you should know it does not choose the worthy. It chooses whoever is holding it when the bell rings, and it has never once been happy with the choice.'],
  ['Thriller', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I have two phones. One for the people I love, and one for the people who might ring at three in the morning. The second one has never rung. I keep it charged anyway. It is a sort of love.'],
  ['*', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You keep saying you did nothing. I believe you. That is what I am angry about.'],
  ['Comedy', 'absurd', 'mono', 2, 'I tried to make friends with the people next door. I took round a cake. They took round a cake. Now we are in some kind of arms race and I have not slept since Tuesday.'],
  ['Horror', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'Every night at three, the phone rings once. I have never answered it. Last night I was awake, and I picked up before it rang, and someone on the line said, "Oh, you are early."'],
  ['Drama', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I can tell the time in this house by the sounds. The boiler at six. The post at nine. The neighbour\'s piano at four, always the same wrong note. If I ever move, I will have to buy a clock.'],
  ['Musical', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'Tonight is my big chance. If I get this wrong, my career is over.'],
  ['War', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I was the one who taught the new boys to dance, in the evenings. Most of them had never held a girl. They held each other, awkwardly, and counted out loud. I still count when I dance.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'They asked if I would like my memories backed up. I said no. I want to be the only one who has them. Some of them should die when I do.'],
  ['*', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'You were the only one who called me by my full name. Everyone else shortened it within a week. You said it every time, all three syllables, as if each one was worth the trouble.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'I have started talking to myself in the supermarket. Not quietly. I hold full meetings. Today I approved the budget for biscuits and then overruled myself on the cheese.'],
  ['Crime', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I found the gun in the bread bin. Of all places. Every morning I had been reaching past it for toast.'],
  ['Drama', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I am going to be very calm. I am going to put this plate down. I am going to put it down very gently, so you understand that I could have done something else with it.'],
  ['Martial arts', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You have studied every one of my fights. You know which side I favour and where I drop my guard. Good. I have studied the people who study me. It is a much shorter list.'],
  ['Period', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 3, 'Every ball I ever went to, I watched from the gallery with a tray. I know every dance by heart. I could lead any one of them. Nobody has ever asked me to, and I think now, at my age, I would only tread on the hem.'],
  ['Fantasy', 'absurd', 'mono', 1, 'I am a magical creature and I have come to grant you three wishes!'],
  ['*', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'My father tells the same joke every Christmas. It is not funny. It has never been funny. If he did not tell it, I think the whole house would fall down.'],
  ['Romance', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'I am not going to ask you to stay. I am going to put the kettle on, and make two cups, and if one of them goes cold, I will know.'],
  ['Thriller', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I know you have been in my flat. You put my shoes back the right way. I always leave them wrong.'],
  ['Drama', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'I passed my driving test on the fourth go. The examiner said "Well done" and I cried in the car for twenty minutes. He sat with me. He did not say anything. I have never been so grateful to a stranger.'],
  ['Horror', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'There is a room in this house with no door. You can see the window from the garden. I have measured the hallways. I know exactly where it is. I put my ear to the wall every night, and every night, someone on the other side does the same.'],
  ['Comedy', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I have perfected the art of leaving a party without saying goodbye. I am so good at it that last week I left my own birthday and nobody noticed for an hour.'],
  ['Sci-fi', 'light', 'mono', 2, 'The aliens have one question for us. They want to know why we wave at boats. I have been asked to prepare an answer. I have been looking at boats for three days. I am no closer.'],
  ['*', 'dark', 'mono', 2, 'I keep my suitcase packed under the bed. I have done since I was nineteen. I have never gone anywhere. I just like knowing the door works.'],
  ['War', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'We must fight for our country. We cannot let the enemy win.'],
  ['Superhero', 'tense', 'mono', 3, 'You want to know the secret? I am not stronger than anyone. I am just the only one who never learned when to stop. They call that a power. My mother called it something else.'],
  ['Drama', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I am sixty-two and I have just learned to ride a bike. I am very bad at it. I fall off at the corner by the post office every Tuesday. The postmistress has started putting a cushion out.'],
  ['Crime', 'tense', 'mono', 1, 'I am innocent! I did not do it! You have to believe me!'],
  ['Western', 'light', 'mono', 3, 'I came west with a wagon, a wife, and an ambition to grow peaches. The wagon broke, the wife left, and the ground out here has never heard of a peach. I grow beans. I tell the beans they are peaches. It seems to help us both.'],
  ['Musical', 'bittersweet', 'mono', 2, 'My father sang in the bath. Only in the bath. The rest of the time, he was the quietest man in {CITY}. I used to sit outside the door on the landing, just to hear what he was really like.'],
]);
